.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-claim 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-claim \- Whether the issue you are about to pull is actually unclaimed
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten claim\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Whether the issue you are about to pull is actually unclaimed
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
batten\-claim\-merged(1)
The keys merged pull request bodies close, as `<key>\\t<number>` rows
.TP
batten\-claim\-keys(1)
The issue keys this branch CLAIMS, as distinct from the ones it merely mentions
.TP
batten\-claim\-check(1)
Refuse a pull of an issue somebody is already on, and mint the receipt when it is free
.TP
batten\-claim\-bot(1)
Attest a bot branch from the lane\*(Aqs public facts, and mint the receipt when they hold
.TP
batten\-claim\-race(1)
Refuse a claim a different open pull request already carries, judged by head SHA
.TP
batten\-claim\-carry(1)
Attest that this branch only carries licence rows forward, and mint the receipt when it does
.TP
batten\-claim\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
